the\nBorel residue `c∞ = (q;q)_∞²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailStar.star_That","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailStar.star_That","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HabiroTailCorollaries.lean#L43-L49","doc":"(★) restated through `That`: the Masbaum tail, normalised, is\n`(−1)ⁿ·T̂_n` at the bar-inverted argument. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailStar.That","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.HabiroTailStar.That","kind":"def","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HabiroTailCorollaries.lean#L38-L41","doc":"The right-hand side of (★), up to its sign:\n`T̂_n(q) = (q;q)_n² · Σ_{k≤n} q^{k(n+1)}·[n,k]_q`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}